To add a file to a folder, the explorer first looks the folder up by id. Adding to the root works, but adding to any nested folder fails because `findFolder` returns `null`. Why?

```js
function findFolder(node, id) {
  if (node.id === id) return node;
  for (const child of node.children ?? []) {
    findFolder(child, id);
  }
  return null;
}
```

What does this log?

```js
const tree = { name: 'src', children: [
  { name: 'index.js' },
  { name: 'utils', children: [{ name: 'math.js' }] },
  { name: 'assets', children: [] },
]};

function paths(node, prefix = '') {
  const here = prefix + node.name;
  if (!node.children) return [here];
  return node.children.flatMap((c) => paths(c, here + '/'));
}

console.log(paths(tree));
```

