In Connect Four, `board` is an array of 6 rows, each an array of 7 cells. After a drop, the game counts matching pieces in each direction with this helper. Horizontal checks work, but dropping a piece into the bottom row and counting downwards (`dr = 1, dc = 0`) crashes. Why?

```js
function count(board, r, c, dr, dc, p) {
  let n = 0;
  while (board[r][c] === p) {
    n++;
    r += dr;
    c += dc;
  }
  return n;
}
```

Follow-up: "Detect a win on an N x N tic-tac-toe board in O(1) per move." You keep sums for each row and column and for both diagonals: +1 for X and -1 for O. A player wins when any sum reaches `±n`. What goes in the blank?

```js
function move(r, c, player) {
  const v = player === 'X' ? 1 : -1;
  rows[r] += v;
  cols[c] += v;
  if (r === c) diag += v;
  if (/* ??? */) anti += v;
  return [rows[r], cols[c], diag, anti].some((s) => Math.abs(s) === n) ? player : null;
}
```

An interviewer asks for an O(1)-space version, and the candidate writes this. What do `isPal('aba')` and `isPal('')` return?

```js
function isPal(s) {
  let i = 0, j = s.length;
  while (i < j) {
    if (s[i] !== s[j]) return false;
    i++;
    j--;
  }
  return true;
}
```

