Todo titles are typed in by users. With this code the page always shows "Failed: HTTP undefined". Which two changes fix the real bugs? (Choose two.)

```js
async function renderTodos(list) {
  try {
    const res = fetch('/api/todos');
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + res.status);
    const todos = await res.json();
    for (const t of todos) list.innerHTML += '<li>' + t.title + '</li>';
  } catch (err) {
    list.textContent = 'Failed: ' + err.message;
  }
}
```

`render(node)` turns data such as the tree below into real DOM nodes. `children` can be a string, an array that mixes strings and nodes, or missing. Text from the data must always appear as text, never be parsed as HTML. The function begins:

```js
// { type: 'ul', props: { class: 'list' }, children: [
//   { type: 'li', children: 'One' },
//   { type: 'li', children: ['Two ', { type: 'b', children: 'bold' }] },
//   { type: 'li', children: [{ type: 'br' }] } ] }
function render(node) {
  if (typeof node === 'string' || typeof node === 'number') {
    return document.createTextNode(String(node));
  }
  const el = document.createElement(node.type);
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(node.props ?? {})) el.setAttribute(k, v);
  /* children handling goes here */
  return el;
}
```

